/strong> <strong>in public law</strong> indicates the text of a measure is contained in the public law text of a bill that became law. For example, the text of <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8878/related-bills/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">H.R. 8878</a> is contained in the text of <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6644/related-bills/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">H.R.6644</a>, which became Public Law 119-101.</li>\n<li>A note highlighting the relationship appears in <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/search?q=%7B%22source%22%3A%22legislation%22%2C%22search%22%3A%22relatedBillType%3A%5C%22Contained+in+public+law%5C%22%22%7D\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">search results</a> and in the <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3341/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">bill overview</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Reintroduction</strong> links two bills in consecutive Congresses having the same official title, same sponsor, and introduced text versions that are identical or nearly identical. For example, <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/9268/related-bills/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">H.R. 9268</a> from the 117th Congress was reintroduced as <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/1318/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">H.R.1318</a> in the 118th Congress.</li>\n<li>Learn more at <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/help/related-bills/?loclr=eacdg\" rel=\"noopener\"","source":"US Congress","published":"2026-08-10T14:23:28+00:00"}],"State (Massachusetts)":[{"title":"S 1485: An Act providing for safe and consensual sensitive examinations","short_title":"An Act providing for safe and consensual sensitive examinations","link":"https://malegislature.gov/Bills/194/S1485.pdf","summary":"Accompanied a new draft, see S3197","source":"State (Massachuse